  {
    "@id": "https://www.musicaintima.org/event-details/wait-list-cognitive-dissonance",
    "http://ogp.me/ns#title": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "WAIT-LIST Cognitive Dissonance | musica intima"
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p><strong>WAIT LIST FOR COGNITIVE DISSONANCE: </strong><em><strong>We will be in touch if/when tickets become available in order received</strong></em></p>\n<p></p>\n<p>This special concert hosted at the Bill Reid Gallery of Northwest Coast Art in downtown Vancouver, one of Vancouver’s Indigenous artistic landmarks, is a sonic offering honouring this continent’s occupied lands and waters, as we centre the voices and stories of its first peoples.</p>\n<p>The programme includes the world premieres of new works by Cree composer <strong>V. Jessica Sparvier-Wells</strong> and Sḵwx̱wú7mesh and Stó:lō, Hawaiian, Swiss interdisciplinary artist <strong>T’uy’t’tanat-Cease Wyss</strong>. Other works include compositions by Cree composers <strong>Andrew Balfour</strong> and <strong>Sherryl Sewapagaham</strong>, as well as Métis composer <strong>Ian Cusson</strong>.</p>\n<p>Curated by Cree-Métis baritone <strong>Jonathon Adams</strong>, this special concert will feature Adams, the voices of musica intima, virtuoso mandolinist <strong>Alon Sariel,</strong> EMV&#39;s summer Artist-in-Residence, the students of Sariel&#39;s workshop &#34;Unconventional Bach&#34;, and flautist Sparvier-Wells.</p>\n<p>Please join us for this free event at 7:30pm on Saturday, August 3rd.</p>\n<p></p>"
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#image": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://static.wixstatic.com/media/5c413d_86dac3d92993462e96cb99003d7cda9e~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c/5c413d_86dac3d92993462e96cb99003d7cda9e~mv2.png"
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#image:width": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "1920"
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#image:height": [
